          "icon": "👍"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "rule",
      "num": 2,
      "title": "2 · TH al final",
      "title_en": "TH at the end",
      "icon": "👄",
      "es": "Al final de palabra, la TH es casi siempre sorda: mouth, both, math, tooth, north, south. Los hispanohablantes tienden a <mark>comérsela o cambiarla por s o t</mark>. Termina con la lengua entre los dientes y deja salir el aire: <code>mauz</code>, no «maus» (¡ratón!).",
      "en": "At the end of a word, TH is almost always voiceless. Don't drop it or change it into S or T.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "mouth",
